MENTOR: That's right. Frame 30 is 1 second, the middle of a move that runs from 0.5 to 1.5 s. Easy Ease puts the peak in the middle like that.

I tried to grab the frame at 1 s to show you where Title is, but it came back blank. So I can't tell you where Title is on screen, and I'll stick to the graph.

**How shaping works:** In the speed graph, each key has a handle. How far it reaches sideways is the **influence**, which sets how long the ease lasts. Easy Ease gives every key the same reach, so every move feels the same.

- **A short reach out of the first key** (0.5 s) means the move gets going quickly.
- **A long reach into the landing key** (1.5 s) means it slows down gradually and lands softly.

That moves the peak toward the start of the move.

Keep the landing handle **on the bottom of the graph** and drag it sideways only. Dragging it up makes Title arrive still moving.

Give it a try on all four moves: each Position move and the Scale. Aim for a short ease out and a long ease in, then say "done". If you'd like to see me shape one first, just ask.
